
---
import Navigation from "../../components/navigation.astro";
import { posts } from "../../data/posts.js";

const post = posts.find((post) => post.slug === "post_eleven");

if (!post) {
  throw new Error("Blog post not found.");
}

const { title, date, tags } = post;
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>{title} | Ivy Duncan</title>
    <meta name="description" content={post.excerpt} />
  </head>

  <body>
    <Navigation />

    <main>
      <article class="blog-post">
        <div class="container narrow">
          <header class="post-header">
            <p class="eyebrow">From the Blog</p>

            <h1>{title}</h1>

            <p class="post-date">{date}</p>

            <div class="post-tags">
              {tags.map((tag) => (
                <a
                  href={`/blog/tag/${tag.toLowerCase().replace(/\s+/g, "-")}`}
                  class="post-tag"
                >
                  {tag}
                </a>
              ))}
            </div>
          </header>

          <div class="post-content">
            <p class="review-intro">
              A quick review of <em>The Yandere Villain Heard My Thoughts</em>.
            </p>

            <figure class="book-cover">
              <img
                src="/images/blog/book_review_one.jpg"
                alt="Cover of The Yandere Villain Heard My Thoughts"
              />
              <figcaption>The Yandere Villain Heard My Thoughts</figcaption>
            </figure>

            <section class="book-details" aria-label="Book details">
              <div class="rating">
                <span class="detail-label">My Rating</span>
                <span class="rating-score">3 <span class="rating-out-of">/ 5 stars</span></span>
              </div>

              <div class="detail-row">
                <span class="detail-label">Where I bought it</span>
                <p>
                  Amazon. I'm a very faithful Barnes &amp; Noble member, but
                  they didn't sell this book.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="detail-row">
                <span class="detail-label">Where I heard about it</span>
                <p>Pinterest</p>
              </div>
            </section>

            <section class="review-section">
              <h2>The Plot</h2>

              <p>
                A guy is transmigrated to an imperial-China-like setting from
                a book he had read (I love this type of shit. Very <em>Lord of Mysteries</em> / <em>Omniscient Reader's Viewpoint</em>-esque),
                and the villain from that book is able to hear his thoughts.
                Including the filthy ones he has about the villain (an imperial
                prince whose fate is to kill lots of people and then die
                alone—this isn't really a spoiler, I promise) because this man
                is supposedly hot af.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section class="review-section">
              <h2>My Thoughts</h2>

              <p>
                This gave me enough entertainment that I read it in a few days,
                but it was more of a fun, fast, one-time read than something
                I'll return to again.
              </p>

              <p>
                It was very consensual (sexually), but it did address consent
                on a deeper level (just because you hear me think something
                doesn't mean that's what I actually want you to do; just
                because you have the power to fix something for me doesn't
                mean you should do it without asking me, etc.).
              </p>

              <p>
                It even made me laugh a few times, and the banter between the
                main characters was enjoyable.
              </p>
            </section>
          </div>

          <footer class="post-footer">
            <a href="/blog" class="back-link">← Back to the blog</a>
          </footer>
        </div>
      </article>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <div class="container">
        <p>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Ivy Duncan. All rights reserved.</p>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .container {
    width: min(1100px, calc(100% - 3rem));
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .narrow {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .blog-post {
    padding: 5rem 0;
  }

  .post-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #765f48;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .post-header h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .post-date {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    color: #6f6a63;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .post-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .post-tag {
    color: #765f48;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .post-tag:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .post-content {
    color: #3f3a35;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .post-content p {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .review-intro {
    text-align: center;
    color: #6f6a63;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .book-cover {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 180px;
    margin: 2rem auto 2.5rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .book-cover img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 4px;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgb(63 58 53 / 12%);
  }

  .book-cover figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    color: #6f6a63;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .book-details {
    margin: 2rem 0 3rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: #f7f3ed;
    border: 1px solid #e8dfd3;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .rating {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd6cd;
  }

  .detail-label {
    display: block;
    color: #765f48;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .rating-score {
    color: #765f48;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .rating-out-of {
    color: #6f6a63;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .detail-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(150px, 0.8fr) 1.5fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .detail-row + .detail-row {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #e8dfd3;
  }

  .detail-row p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .review-section {
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
  }

  .review-section h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #765f48;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .post-footer {
    margin-top: 4rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #ddd6cd;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: #765f48;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .site-footer {
    padding: 2rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #ddd6cd;
    color: #6f6a63;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .container {
      width: min(100% - 2rem, 1100px);
    }

    .blog-post {
      padding: 3.5rem 0;
    }

    .book-details {
      padding: 1.25rem;
    }

    .detail-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.35rem;
    }
  }
</style>